  "worked_solution": "The complement of $K,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{K},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $K.$ To represent $\\overset{\u2015}{K},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $K,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/assets/74345aeb2a1028e07d155dd357a9bb412860309c99cee37c62380907b3e1bd37.png)\n\nThe element in the shaded area is $n.$ This is the only element of $U$ that is not in $K.$ Therefore, the complement of $K$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{K}={n}.\n$$",
